        /// Live syncs are included in the monthly price of the connection, like the automatic syncs: nothing extra is charged. The only limit is the bank's. Banks limit reads without the person present, for example to four a day (the Didit Test Bank in sandbox does the same). The automatic syncs of the day (<c>sync.frequency_per_day</c>) are set aside first and the rest are yours, so <c>sync.budgets</c> shows what is left and <c>sync.live_syncs_left_today</c> how many live syncs remain today. The automatic schedule never uses the last two reads of a day, so two live syncs always remain. When the budget is used up the call answers <c>429 refresh_limit_reached</c> with <c>Retry-After</c> (the seconds until the budget resets, 1 to 86400) and a <c>sync</c> object with <c>live_syncs_left_today</c> and <c>budgets</c>. The limit is a ceiling set by the bank, not a promise of a number of syncs.
        /// <para/>
        /// When a sync stores changes, <c>bank.data.updated</c> tells you; then read the change feed.
        /// <para/>
        /// Needs an API key with the Bank data permission (<c>bank-data</c>): write for this operation, which changes something. A key with full access does not include it: grant it explicitly when you create the key, or the call answers <c>403 bank_data_access_denied</c>.
        /// <para/>
        /// Refreshing a deleted connection answers <c>409 connection_not_active</c>.
        /// <para/>
        /// <c>POST /v3/bank/connections/{id}/refresh/</c> (<c>bank.refresh_connection</c>).
        /// Accepts an idempotency key: set <see cref="RequestOptions.IdempotencyKey"/>.
        /// </remarks>
        /// <param name="id">The connection id.</param>
        /// <param name="parameters">The request parameters.</param>
        /// <param name="requestOptions">Per-request overrides of the client options.</param>
        /// <param name="cancellationToken">Cancels the request.</param>
        public async Task<BankRefreshConnectionResponse> RefreshConnectionAsync(string id, BankRefreshRequest? parameters = null, RequestOptions? requestOptions = null, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
        {
            var response = await _raw.RefreshConnectionAsync(id, parameters, requestOptions, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);
            return response.Data;
        }

        /// <summary>
        /// Renew a bank connection
        /// </summary>
        /// <remarks>
        /// Creates a renew link for this connection, a shortcut for <c>create_link</c> with <c>mode: renew</c>. The connection id and every account id stay the same.
        /// <para/>
        /// Opening the returned link on the hosted page is not available yet: the page that lets the person renew is still to be built.
        /// <para/>
        /// Until the consent has 30 days left or fewer it answers <c>409 renewal_not_needed</c>; after <c>consent.renewable_until</c> it answers <c>409 renewal_window_expired</c> and the person connects again.
        /// <para/>
        /// Needs an API key with the Bank data permission (<c>bank-data</c>): write for this operation, which changes something. A key with full access does not include it: grant it explicitly when you create the key, or the call answers <c>403 bank_data_access_denied</c>.
        /// <para/>
        /// <c>POST /v3/bank/connections/{id}/renew/</c> (<c>bank.renew_connection</c>).
        /// Accepts an idempotency key: set <see cref="RequestOptions.IdempotencyKey"/>.
        /// </remarks>
        /// <param name="id">The connection id.</param>
        /// <param name="parameters">The request parameters.</param>
        /// <param name="requestOptions">Per-request overrides of the client options.</param>
        /// <param name="cancellationToken">Cancels the request.</param>
        public async Task<BankLink> RenewConnectionAsync(string id, BankRenewLinkRequest? parameters = null, RequestOptions? requestOptions = null, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
        {
